Read, replace, and delete items in an existing State Store. Items in user-isolated stores require a hosted call ID and cannot be accessed by azd.

Usage
  azd ai agent state-stores items [command]

Available Commands
  delete : Delete an item from an existing store.
  list   : List one page of item keys and metadata, without values.
  set    : Create or replace a JSON object item in an existing store.
  show   : Show an item's JSON value, tags, and ETag.

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for items
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (default "default")

Examples
    azd ai agent state-stores items list
    azd ai agent state-stores items show task-123

Use azd ai agent state-stores items [command] --help to view examples and more information about a specific command.
